[{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/pi0_decay/#π-γ-γ-in-the-laboratory","page":"Neutral pion decay","text":"This tutorial walks through a minimal four-momentum exercise for neutral pion decay. Photon energies match half the π⁰ mass in the decay frame (m_pi0/2), boosted with Bz into the lab, rotated with Ry and Rz so that photon 1 aligns with the parent kinematics (spherical_coordinates), and complemented by subtraction for photon 2.\n\nusing FourVectors\nusing Test","title":"π⁰ → γ γ in the laboratory"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/pi0_decay/#Mass-units-and-laboratory-pion","page":"Neutral pion decay","text":"Approximate π⁰ mass in GeV; lab three-momentum is chosen as a simple illustrative example.\n\nm_pi0 = 0.135\np_pi0 = FourVector(1.0, 1.0, 30.0; M = m_pi0)\n\n4-element FourVector{Float64} with indices SOneTo(4):\n  1.0\n  1.0\n 30.0\n 30.033618246891265","title":"Mass units and laboratory pion"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/pi0_decay/#Photon-1-—-scale-(massless-proxy),-lab-boost,-rotations-to-match-the-parent-axis","page":"Neutral pion decay","text":"Pick polar angle theta_gamma along (sin θ, 0, cos θ). The factor m_pi0/2 sets the invariant mass squared to zero for the auxiliary FourVector; then apply Bz(boost_gamma(p_pi0)) and rotations using acos(Omega.cosθ) and Omega.ϕ where Omega = spherical_coordinates(p_pi0) encodes the pion pointing direction.\n\ntheta_gamma = 0.3\nOmega = spherical_coordinates(p_pi0)\n\np_gamma1 =\n    let\n        p = (m_pi0 / 2) * FourVector(sin(theta_gamma), 0.0, cos(theta_gamma); E = 1.0)\n        p |> Bz(boost_gamma(p_pi0)) |> Ry(acos(Omega.cosθ)) |> Rz(Omega.ϕ)\n    end\n\n4-element FourVector{Float64} with indices SOneTo(4):\n  0.9917625170514055\n  0.9917625170514054\n 29.329252809918138\n 29.36276989945852\n\nPhoton 2 restores four-momentum: p_gamma1 + p_gamma2 ≈ p_pi0.\n\np_gamma2 = p_pi0 - p_gamma1\n\n@test mass2(p_gamma1) < 1e-10\n@test mass2(p_gamma2) < 1e-10\n@test mass(p_gamma1 + p_gamma2) ≈ mass(p_pi0)\n@test p_gamma1 + p_gamma2 ≈ p_pi0\n\nTest Passed","title":"Photon 1 — scale (massless proxy), lab boost, rotations to match the parent axis"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/pi0_decay/#Quick-inspection","page":"Neutral pion decay","text":"(collect(p_pi0), collect(p_gamma1), collect(p_gamma2))\n\n([1.0, 1.0, 30.0, 30.033618246891265], [0.9917625170514055, 0.9917625170514054, 29.329252809918138, 29.36276989945852], [0.008237482948594499, 0.00823748294859461, 0.6707471900818618, 0.6708483474327451])","title":"Quick inspection"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/#API-reference","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"API reference"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#FourVectors.Bz-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{FourVector{T}, T}} where T","page":"API reference","text":"Bz(p::FourVector{T}, γ::T) where {T}\n\nApplies an active boost along the z-axis with Lorentz factor γ. A negative γ reverses the boost direction (same |γ|, opposite sign of longitudinal velocity).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FourVectors.Bz"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#FourVectors.Rx-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{FourVector{T}, T}} where T","page":"API reference","text":"Rx(p::FourVector{T}, α::T) where {T}\n\nApplies an active rotation by angle α about the x-axis to p.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FourVectors.Rx"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#FourVectors.Ry-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{FourVector{T}, T}} where T","page":"API reference","text":"Ry(p::FourVector{T}, θ::T) where {T}\n\nApplies an active rotation by angle θ about the y-axis to p.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FourVectors.Ry"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#FourVectors.Rz-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{FourVector{T}, T}} where T","page":"API reference","text":"Rz(p::FourVector{T}, ϕ::T) where {T}\n\nApplies an active rotation by angle ϕ about the z-axis to p.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FourVectors.Rz"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#FourVectors.rotate_to_plane-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"rotate_to_plane(p, which_z, which_xplus)\n\nRotates a four-momentum p into a reference frame where the z-axis follows which_z and where the spatial direction which_xplus fixes azimuth (φ > 0 half-plane).\n\nSequence:\n\nRotate so which_z aligns with the lab +z (Ry, Rz).\nRotate about z so which_xplus sits in the x–z plane at non-negative x.\n\nExample\n\njulia> p = FourVector(0.5, 0.5, 0.5; M = 1.0);\n\njulia> which_z = FourVector(0.0, 0.0, 1.0; M = 2.0);\n\njulia> which_xplus = FourVector(1.0, 1.0, 0.0; M = 0.0);\n\njulia> rotate_to_plane(p, which_z, which_xplus)\n4-element FourVector{Float64} with indices SOneTo(4):\n 0.7071067811865475\n 5.551115123125783e-17\n 0.5\n 1.3228756555322954\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FourVectors.rotate_to_plane"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#FourVectors.spherical_coordinates-Tuple{Any}","page":"API reference","text":"spherical_coordinates(p)\n\nPolar direction of spatial part of p as (cosθ = cos_theta(p), ϕ = azimuthal_angle(p)).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FourVectors.spherical_coordinates"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#FourVectors.transform_to_cmf-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"transform_to_cmf(p, which_cmf)\n\nTransforms p into the center-of-momentum frame of which_cmf: rotate so its spatial direction aligns with +z, then boost along z using the Lorentz factor of which_cmf.\n\nExample\n\njulia> p = FourVector(0.5, 0.5, 0.5; M = 1.0);\n\njulia> transform_to_cmf(p, FourVector(1.0, 0.0, 0.0; E = 2.0))\n4-element FourVector{Float64} with indices SOneTo(4):\n -0.49999999999999994\n  0.5\n -0.18641234663634787\n  1.238850097057134\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FourVectors.transform_to_cmf"},{"category":"section","location":"#FourVectors.jl","page":"Home","text":"FourVectors wraps an immutable Cartesian four-momentum (FourVector as FieldVector{4}) and implements the LorentzVectorBase.jl interface.\n\nInstallation, exported kinematic accessors, and usage examples appear in the README on GitHub (README.md).","title":"FourVectors.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Guides","page":"Home","text":"See Neutral pion decay.\n\nSource Julia script: literate/tutorials/pi0_decay.jl. It is bundled into this manual with Literate.jl and its code chunks are executed during docs/make.jl when the manual is built.","title":"Guides"}]
